  "question": {
    "math_academy_id": "q-127260",
    "knowledge_point_id": "d8297713-fb86-59f2-af4d-850af2575541",
    "knowledge_point": "Calculating the Expected Value for a Random Variable with Non-Uniform Probability",
    "problem": "The absolute difference between the outcomes of one roll of two fair tetrahedral dice follows the probability mass function $f(x)$ shown in the table below. What is the expected value of the absolute difference of the outcomes of one roll of the two dice?\n\n| $f(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |",
    "worked_solution": "The expected value of a discrete random variable $X$ with probability mass function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X]={\\sum }_{x\\in S}x\\cdot f(x).\n$$\n\nSumming up the products of each value of $X$ and its associated probability, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot f(0)+1\\cdot f(1)+2\\cdot f(2)+3\\cdot f(3) \\\\  & =0(\\frac{1}{4})+1(\\frac{3}{8})+2(\\frac{1}{4})+3(\\frac{1}{8}) \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{2}{4}+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{3}{8}+\\frac{4}{8}+\\frac{3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{0+3+4+3}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
